utput_tokens":872201,"reasoning_output_tokens":304469,"total_tokens":295459788},"turn_id":"01a101c3-e32d-7580-ba72-be0d3d17ace2","turn_token_usage":{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":4553344,"input_tokens":4585182,"output_tokens":18731,"reasoning_output_tokens":6807,"total_tokens":4603913},"usage":{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":210048,"input_tokens":210882,"output_tokens":5887,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":216769}},"message":"","previous_window_id":"01a1019c-223a-7962-9f39-917118cea9e3","replacement_history":[{"content":[{"text":"Start from branch `codex/mos-aster-racing-city` in `entireio/marvin`. Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/simulator-agent-rules.md`, and follow those instructions throughout the session.\n\nInspect the branch and working tree without discarding changes. Fetch the remote and update safely if needed. Follow the Entire session attachment and trailer verification requirements for every commit.\n\nThen ask me: **“What would you like to work on next?”** Wait for my answer before making changes.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fd98-3767-7440-ade8-38af43a729d1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790961006.439423,"turn_id":"01a0fd98-3151-7b32-a2f4-a06fc6d958d7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The sound design is awful. None of the droids have a driving sound that gets louder with higher speeds. No boost sound either. Instead, they just make way too many squeaking noises. The city is quiet as well. The race is a joke. Your goal is to fix this and implement a sound design that matches AAA game. Use a judge on Codex Astra Ultra to make sure you don’t deliver poor work again.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fd9b-bc4e-7812-a19a-70a924aec95a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790961237.070703,"turn_id":"01a0fd9b-bbfd-77b1-bd1a-3963a2bc9694"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Don’t forget the sand storm and sounds for it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fda7-7970-7352-90e0-116ed229ecd5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790962006.384774,"turn_id":"01a0fd9b-bbfd-77b1-bd1a-3963a2bc9694"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What's the scratching noise that Marvin is making and why does WALL-E sound like a screwdriver?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fddf-bdcc-7471-990a-9a609331cae2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790965693.900144,"turn_id":"01a0fddf-bb06-7f53-8a99-51781430bbb0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The judge compared that to real WALL-E and thought it fits? I have a hard time believing that. The boost sounds awful too. Anyway, another round please. Also, when driving through narrow gaps in the city, the POV camera does weird things. Also also, the track edge has two holes near the gate. Fix all these. \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fde3-a619-7c60-ad82-46c3287376aa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790965949.977842,"turn_id":"01a0fde3-a5a7-79e1-9f62-f5e0396645ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Treat the exit to the service area the same as the exit at the gate.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fdf9-b564-7b60-a71a-f325b58f78df","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790967395.684576,"turn_id":"01a0fde3-a5a7-79e1-9f62-f5e0396645ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The ramp is too obviously separated from the infield area. That’s not how sand works.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fe1c-590e-7f02-a0cc-53c00ee5399d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790969665.806971,"turn_id":"01a0fde3-a5a7-79e1-9f62-f5e0396645ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"wtf, now you created a hard line between ramp and track that makes no sense","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fe35-af6e-7050-a678-7b877e1cbefd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790971326.318149,"turn_id":"01a0fde3-a5a7-79e1-9f62-f5e0396645ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Why do we have to discuss the same problems over and over again?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fe36-bd1a-70d2-9d31-d38789ef9048","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790971395.354139,"turn_id":"01a0fde3-a5a7-79e1-9f62-f5e0396645ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Next, measure the frame rate when driving through town. Are we still at a constant 60fps? It felt a bit stuttery on my MacBook Air M4.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fe37-1635-7041-acb3-c412009588f1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790971418.165391,"turn_id":"01a0fe37-15f1-7f22-b4a5-b0a4836328aa"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The track also should now have a shoulder on the exit ramp","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fe37-7229-7af3-a5f9-b5f705f164cb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790971441.705806,"turn_id":"01a0fe37-71f5-7f73-b5da-71ca5eb76b98"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Compare both ramps off the track. Show me aerial shots and judge them.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fe37-fdee-7b32-9c59-d2f2bd2b46b9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790971477.486852,"turn_id":"01a0fe37-71f5-7f73-b5da-71ca5eb76b98"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Fix it then for both ramps.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fe62-2ccc-7c12-8273-6626b91c859a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790974241.996603,"turn_id":"01a0fe62-2ca0-73d3-8f61-55bf53020098"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Next, measure the frame rate when driving through town. Are we still at a constant 60fps? It felt a bit stuttery on my MacBook Air M4.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fea0-5109-7ea0-b58d-5c05772ee627","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790978314.505465,"turn_id":"01a0fea0-4eb6-70f2-aa7d-fd496fc9f73c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Next, measure the frame rate when driving through town. Are we still at a constant 60fps? It felt a bit stuttery on my MacBook Air M4.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fea1-02c7-7842-ab65-dd6d75e27248","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790978360.007394,"turn_id":"01a0fea0-4eb6-70f2-aa7d-fd496fc9f73c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Debut the slowdown","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fea8-c035-7ca1-8636-8cfc2415897e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790978867.25378,"turn_id":"01a0fea8-bff8-7e70-8654-2b91708877ae"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Can you add the frame rate to the UI?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fee5-a806-72e1-bdce-0664153be778","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790982858.758679,"turn_id":"01a0fee5-a52e-7a71-8527-fba9fa665dc4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Now play for 10min. Does the shown fps stay at 60?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fefd-e1f6-7520-9f27-2f34c57a2a3d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790984446.454271,"turn_id":"01a0fefd-def9-7e91-bda8-194ba5f4e43f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ok, so where did you go wrong given you claimed no frame rate drops for days now?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ff0e-aae2-7711-a01f-7a34654ce47c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790985546.466529,"turn_id":"01a0fefd-def9-7e91-bda8-194ba5f4e43f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Make a plan to fix it, fix it, validate it, and add proper testing so this never happens again. Your goal is to achieve constant 60fps over 10min without reducing the game’s level of details. In fact, we need more headroom to achieve even higher quality.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ff17-16fe-70b0-9e82-e7a56a21a149","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790986098.430386,"turn_id":"01a0ff17-13fd-7563-b654-73f8e5d3ea82"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Doesn’t Apple provide tooling to measure this instead of you doing wild guesses?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ff9f-ca47-7263-86e9-a71d4999b839","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790995057.223647,"turn_id":"01a0ff17-13fd-7563-b654-73f8e5d3ea82"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Request the screen recording permissions please","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ffae-bd5e-7fb3-abce-5298ca8dbd7f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790996036.958577,"turn_id":"01a0ffae-bb32-7c53-9633-3bbcff43ec56"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"You are not requesting it. You are bringing up a custom UI that I can’t use.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ffaf-9863-77e3-942b-d5fbd873c477","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790996093.0277,"turn_id":"01a0ffaf-9832-7720-bb5d-8398e36192a5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ok, open the custom UI again please\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ffc9-0e39-7e43-9fc1-fe890c555c56","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790997761.593374,"turn_id":"01a0ffc9-0bf0-7b90-957f-a502a6a33599"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_lILC0ZpASbuY4y6qqtpiGywP\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"May I install Apple’s free Xcode app from the Mac App Store? The HUD reports use generic encoder names; Xcode’s Metal debugger and Instruments would let me inspect the actual shaders, resource uploads, and CPU/GPU scheduling. Apple lists a 3.1 GB download, with additional disk space needed after installation.\",\"answer\":\"Install Xcode\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ffd8-c182-7573-b185-e73fd1178620","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790998790.530343,"turn_id":"01a0ffc9-0bf0-7b90-957f-a502a6a33599"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Yes\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ffe1-0b58-7a61-8257-fe01c4b762e3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790999333.720382,"turn_id":"01a0ffe1-0949-71c2-b88a-50af964eee63"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Done","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0ffee-a6e2-7ab1-8f6b-f9337a3ac949","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791000225.506323,"turn_id":"01a0ffee-a66f-78e3-baf3-cc1d16910524"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Okay, and now we wait for what?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fffd-2fb6-78b0-844f-38788c3987af","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791001178.038106,"turn_id":"01a0fffd-2da0-75b1-9ab8-e0b0bd628175"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Should have or are you doing it?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0fffd-88e4-77a3-987d-9ab8590fcf4d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791001200.868506,"turn_id":"01a0fffd-8886-7310-944d-7ba3e2dd48e9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"You are still playing the guessing game. Can you not measure CPU/GPU consumption with full details on what takes how much time?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10186-6106-7e81-86ac-1d3c68650bd1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791026946.310104,"turn_id":"01a10182-70d7-7b71-9c72-962423519979"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ignore my M4. Focus only on this M2.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101ad-2763-7262-9653-e786a36db3d9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791029487.459997,"turn_id":"01a101ab-e536-7c10-a64a-36c533f318c3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Why is the audio taking to much CPU time?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101af-b984-7161-978e-15acc7fd6687","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791029655.94,"turn_id":"01a101ab-e536-7c10-a64a-36c533f318c3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Hm, how many CPU cores can the game use?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101b1-69f2-77b3-ae78-e84b4f4eb729","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791029766.642298,"turn_id":"01a101ab-e536-7c10-a64a-36c533f318c3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cskills_instructions\u003e\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/Users/thomi/.agents/skills`\n- `r1` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r2` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r3` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.16/skills`\n- `r4` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.19/skills`\n- `r5` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r6` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/0.1.75/skills`\n- `r7` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r8` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r9` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.909.12148/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: r1/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including 'you,' 'your,' 'this app,' or 'this coding agent' when they refer to Codex—and for OpenAI APIs/products and ChatGPT Work. Also use for model choice/migration, prompting, SDKs, Responses, Realtime, agents, evals, and Chat/Work/Codex comparisons. Do not use for generic app/software tasks that merely mention Codex. (file: r1/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-creator: Create and scaffold plugin directories for Codex with a required `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, optional plugin folders/files, valid manifest defaults, and personal-marketplace entries by default. Use when Codex needs to create a new personal plugin, add optional plugin structure, generate or update marketplace entries for plugin ordering and availability metadata, or update an existing local plugin during development with the CLI-driven cachebuster and reinstall flow. (file: r1/plugin-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r1/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: r1/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- deploy-release: Deploy a release. Use when shipping a tagged build. Do NOT use when changing unrelated configuration. (file: r0/deploy-release/SKILL.md)\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted document artifacts inside the container, with a strict render-and-verify workflow. Use `render_docx.py` to generate page PNGs (and optional PDF) for visual QA, then iterate until layout is flawless before delivering the final document. (file: r8/documents/26.909.12148/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-docs: Prompt- and template-complete Google Docs creation and editing with explicit-instruction-authoritative structural preservation, including semantic roles, relationships, comparison dimensions, and instructed extensions; full-topology native-copy routing; source-grounded per-tab adaptation for past/example references; style-preserving hyperlink and table edits; canonical smart-chip-first authoring for dates and relevant supported people or Google resources; a file-backed advisory trusted read before existing-document writes; automatic protected-control awareness; direct connector APIs by default; DOCX-first import only when no supplied Google Doc template/reference constrains the output; and checked-in code mode only for exact native dropdown mutation. Use when Codex must create, edit, fill, adapt, redesign, or verify Google Docs without overriding explicit user/template instructions, adding unrequested document scope, or carrying stale reference facts into a new deliverable. (file: r3/google-docs/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive: Use connected Google Drive as the single entrypoint for Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides work. Use when the user wants to find, fetch, organize, share, export, copy, or delete Drive files, or summarize and edit Google Docs, Google Sheets, and Google Slides through one unified Google Drive plugin. (file: r3/google-drive/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive-comments: Write, reply to, and resolve Google Drive comments on Docs, Sheets, Slides, and Drive files with evidence-backed location context. Use when the user asks to leave comments, review a file with comments, respond to comment threads, or resolve Drive comments. (file: r3/google-drive-comments/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-sheets: Analyze and edit connected Google Sheets with range precision. Use when the user wants to create Google Sheets, find a spreadsheet, inspect tabs or ranges, search rows, plan formulas, create or repair charts, clean or restructure tables, write concise summaries, or make explicit cell-range updates. (file: r3/google-sheets/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-slides: Route Google Slides authoring requests and derive a design system from a native template or reference deck. Use this skill when the user provides an existing native Google Slides deck as a template, reference, or prior-period source, or asks to edit, update, repair, restyle, or clean up an existing native Google Slides deck. Use the Presentations skill instead for net-new presentation creation when no existing native Google Slides deck must be followed. (file: r3/google-slides/SKILL.md)\n- pages:maintain-space: Reconcile new evidence into existing ChatGPT Pages or a Space when the user requests upkeep. For a direct text correction, use write-page. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts, writing, or advice, or treat a selected Page as a request to save. Schedule future upkeep only when requested. (file: r4/maintain-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:manage-schedules: Review a ChatGPT Space page and its schedules, recommend useful recurring work, and create, update, or remove scheduled automations. (file: r4/manage-schedules/SKILL.md)\n- pages:organize-space: Organize existing ChatGPT Pages and Space structure when the user requests changes to that structure. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts or advice; a selected Page alone does not authorize reorganization. A narrow text edit does not need this workflow. (file: r4/organize-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:write-page: Create or edit requested Page/Space content, or use for prose you have already decided to save as a standalone Markdown file, only if the user did not explicitly request a Markdown file. Honor established formats, destinations, and repository documentation. A selected Page alone does not authorize a write. (file: r4/write-page/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters, including fillable AcroForms. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: r8/pdf/26.909.12148/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-management:plugin-management: Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit from an external app, account, service, or data source that available tools cannot access. (file: r5/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Read, create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks. Use for presentation, slide deck, PowerPoint, PPT, PPTX, or Google Slides requests. (file: r8/presentations/26.909.12148/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-building: Use Sites when the user wants a complete website built for them, such as a landing page, portfolio, dashboard, portal, tracker, hub, or internal tool, or wants to modify a website built with Sites. Do not use for development work in other web projects unless the user explicitly requests Sites. (file: r6/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Use after `sites-building` to publish new sites and edits, for requested website publishing or deployment, or for hosting management. A project containing `.openai/hosting.json` uses Sites hosting only when the current request concerns that Site. Publishing an npm package or standalone asset is not website publishing. Honor an explicit request to use another hosting provider. (file: r6/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-mcp: Build or update a Site-hosted MCP server and help users access its tools through the Site's plugin in ChatGPT or Codex. (file: r6/sites-mcp/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-preview-troubleshooting: Diagnose and recover failed supervised sites-preview sessions after sites-building. Applies only to the managed-linux execution profile, not portable previews. (file: r6/sites-preview-troubleshooting/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Use skill when user requests to create, modify, analyze, visualize, or work with spreadsheet files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.csv`, `.tsv`) or Google Sheets with formulas, formatting, charts, tables, and recalculation. Do not use for live controlling Microsoft Excel app or a live Excel session. (file: r9/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel task. Do not use for standalone spreadsheet files or Google Sheets. (file: r9/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference document, presentation, spreadsheet, Google Docs, Slides, or Sheets link, ImageGen or Product Design image, email, Slack message, or Site project, or explicitly asks to edit or update a passed artifact-template skill. Do not use for one-off creation from an existing template. (file: r8/template-creator/26.909.12148/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compare or inspect; create simulations, maps, charts, graphs, and mockups. Use standard tools for static scientific figures. (file: r2/visualize/1.0.32/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new ChatGPT Pets, custom mascots, non-pixel styles, and unattached sprite sheets requiring nine animation states plus sixteen look directions. Preserve Library artifacts and Pets MCP lifecycle behavior. Exclude real pets, standalone images, and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `danger-full-access`: No filesystem sandboxing - all commands are permitted. Network access is enabled.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101d3-b36c-7510-9b7f-eb02d595e8aa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions"],"turn_id":"01a101c3-e32d-7580-ba72-be0d3d17ace2"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101d3-b36c-7510-9b7f-eb191bcd9a77","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a101c3-e32d-7580-ba72-be0d3d17ace2"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101d3-b36c-7510-9b7f-eb2bc2586484","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a101c3-e32d-7580-ba72-be0d3d17ace2"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/Users/thomi/Projects\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ezsh\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-03\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eEurope/Berlin\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/Users/thomi/Projects\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"disabled\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"unrestricted\" /\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n  \u003csubagents\u003e\n    - astra_ultra_final_judge: Gibbs\n    - audio_judge: Zeno\n  \u003c/subagents\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101d3-b36c-7510-9b7f-eb341219e7ba","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a101c3-e32d-7580-ba72-be0d3d17ace2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Come up with a plan to optimize the GPU. Do we have too many vertexes? Do we render things that aren’t visible? Are there other game developer techniques to improve this?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a101c1-3e6c-7643-a35c-89d52e434cbf","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791030804.076989,"turn_id":"01a101ab-e536-7c10-a64a-36c533f318c3"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"window_id":"01a101d3-b36b-7100-816e-e549a7c2e304","window_number":17}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T12:53:33.682Z","ordinal":17141,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6-astra","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/Users/thomi/Projects","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-10-03","timezone":"Europe/Berlin","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/thomi/Projects</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>","subagents":"- astra_ultra_final_judge: Gibbs\n- audio_judge: Zeno"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/Users/thomi/.agents/skills`\n- `r1` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r2` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r3` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.16/skills`\n- `r4` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.19/skills`\n- `r5` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r6` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/0.1.75/skills`\n- `r7` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r8` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r9` = `/Users/thomi/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.909.12148/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: r1/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including 'you,' 'your,' 'this app,' or 'this coding agent' when they refer to Codex—and for OpenAI APIs/products and ChatGPT Work. Also use for model choice/migration, prompting, SDKs, Responses, Realtime, agents, evals, and Chat/Work/Codex comparisons. Do not use for generic app/software tasks that merely mention Codex. (file: r1/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-creator: Create and scaffold plugin directories for Codex with a required `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, optional plugin folders/files, valid manifest defaults, and personal-marketplace entries by default. Use when Codex needs to create a new personal plugin, add optional plugin structure, generate or update marketplace entries for plugin ordering and availability metadata, or update an existing local plugin during development with the CLI-driven cachebuster and reinstall flow. (file: r1/plugin-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r1/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: r1/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- deploy-release: Deploy a release. Use when shipping a tagged build. Do NOT use when changing unrelated configuration. (file: r0/deploy-release/SKILL.md)\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted document artifacts inside the container, with a strict render-and-verify workflow. Use `render_docx.py` to generate page PNGs (and optional PDF) for visual QA, then iterate until layout is flawless before delivering the final document. (file: r8/documents/26.909.12148/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-docs: Prompt- and template-complete Google Docs creation and editing with explicit-instruction-authoritative structural preservation, including semantic roles, relationships, comparison dimensions, and instructed extensions; full-topology native-copy routing; source-grounded per-tab adaptation for past/example references; style-preserving hyperlink and table edits; canonical smart-chip-first authoring for dates and relevant supported people or Google resources; a file-backed advisory trusted read before existing-document writes; automatic protected-control awareness; direct connector APIs by default; DOCX-first import only when no supplied Google Doc template/reference constrains the output; and checked-in code mode only for exact native dropdown mutation. Use when Codex must create, edit, fill, adapt, redesign, or verify Google Docs without overriding explicit user/template instructions, adding unrequested document scope, or carrying stale reference facts into a new deliverable. (file: r3/google-docs/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive: Use connected Google Drive as the single entrypoint for Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides work. Use when the user wants to find, fetch, organize, share, export, copy, or delete Drive files, or summarize and edit Google Docs, Google Sheets, and Google Slides through one unified Google Drive plugin. (file: r3/google-drive/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive-comments: Write, reply to, and resolve Google Drive comments on Docs, Sheets, Slides, and Drive files with evidence-backed location context. Use when the user asks to leave comments, review a file with comments, respond to comment threads, or resolve Drive comments. (file: r3/google-drive-comments/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-sheets: Analyze and edit connected Google Sheets with range precision. Use when the user wants to create Google Sheets, find a spreadsheet, inspect tabs or ranges, search rows, plan formulas, create or repair charts, clean or restructure tables, write concise summaries, or make explicit cell-range updates. (file: r3/google-sheets/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-slides: Route Google Slides authoring requests and derive a design system from a native template or reference deck. Use this skill when the user provides an existing native Google Slides deck as a template, reference, or prior-period source, or asks to edit, update, repair, restyle, or clean up an existing native Google Slides deck. Use the Presentations skill instead for net-new presentation creation when no existing native Google Slides deck must be followed. (file: r3/google-slides/SKILL.md)\n- pages:maintain-space: Reconcile new evidence into existing ChatGPT Pages or a Space when the user requests upkeep. For a direct text correction, use write-page. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts, writing, or advice, or treat a selected Page as a request to save. Schedule future upkeep only when requested. (file: r4/maintain-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:manage-schedules: Review a ChatGPT Space page and its schedules, recommend useful recurring work, and create, update, or remove scheduled automations. (file: r4/manage-schedules/SKILL.md)\n- pages:organize-space: Organize existing ChatGPT Pages and Space structure when the user requests changes to that structure. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts or advice; a selected Page alone does not authorize reorganization. A narrow text edit does not need this workflow. (file: r4/organize-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:write-page: Create or edit requested Page/Space content, or use for prose you have already decided to save as a standalone Markdown file, only if the user did not explicitly request a Markdown file. Honor established formats, destinations, and repository documentation. A selected Page alone does not authorize a write. (file: r4/write-page/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters, including fillable AcroForms. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: r8/pdf/26.909.12148/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-management:plugin-management: Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit from an external app, account, service, or data source that available tools cannot access. (file: r5/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Read, create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks. Use for presentation, slide deck, PowerPoint, PPT, PPTX, or Google Slides requests. (file: r8/presentations/26.909.12148/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-building: Use Sites when the user wants a complete website built for them, such as a landing page, portfolio, dashboard, portal, tracker, hub, or internal tool, or wants to modify a website built with Sites. Do not use for development work in other web projects unless the user explicitly requests Sites. (file: r6/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Use after `sites-building` to publish new sites and edits, for requested website publishing or deployment, or for hosting management. A project containing `.openai/hosting.json` uses Sites hosting only when the current request concerns that Site. Publishing an npm package or standalone asset is not website publishing. Honor an explicit request to use another hosting provider. (file: r6/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-mcp: Build or update a Site-hosted MCP server and help users access its tools through the Site's plugin in ChatGPT or Codex. (file: r6/sites-mcp/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-preview-troubleshooting: Diagnose and recover failed supervised sites-preview sessions after sites-building. Applies only to the managed-linux execution profile, not portable previews. (file: r6/sites-preview-troubleshooting/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Use skill when user requests to create, modify, analyze, visualize, or work with spreadsheet files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.csv`, `.tsv`) or Google Sheets with formulas, formatting, charts, tables, and recalculation. Do not use for live controlling Microsoft Excel app or a live Excel session. (file: r9/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel task. Do not use for standalone spreadsheet files or Google Sheets. (file: r9/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference document, presentation, spreadsheet, Google Docs, Slides, or Sheets link, ImageGen or Product Design image, email, Slack message, or Site project, or explicitly asks to edit or update a passed artifact-template skill. Do not use for one-off creation from an existing template. (file: r8/template-creator/26.909.12148/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compare or inspect; create simulations, maps, charts, graphs, and mockups. Use standard tools for static scientific figures. (file: r2/visualize/1.0.32/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new ChatGPT Pets, custom mascots, non-pixel styles, and unattached sprite sheets requiring nine animation states plus sixteen look directions. Preserve Library artifacts and Pets MCP lifecycle behavior. Exclude real pets, standalone images, and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n","includeInstructions":true},"managed_developer_instructions":{},"model":"gpt-6-astra","multi_agent_mode":{"mode":"explicitRequestOnly","usage_hint_hash":"30fb77255ffd0abcecb08a8897e242564dfe1192"},"multi_agent_usage_hint":"30fb77255ffd0abcecb08a8897e242564dfe1192","orchestrator_skills":{"includeInstructions":true,"enabled":false},"permissions":{"instructions":"32ca25d6d85edaeb6f1e19b2a5cc4e08d2a631cd","approved_command_prefixes":[["/bin/zsh","-lc","'apps/simulator-macos/.build/Marvin Simulator.app/Contents/MacOS/MarvinSimulator' --town-smoke-test /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/brick-walls-final > /tmp/marvin-brick-smoke.log 2>&1"],["/bin/zsh","-lc","'apps/simulator-macos/.build/Marvin Simulator.app/Contents/M