{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:36:45.911Z","ordinal":17942,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","turn_id":"01a101fa-8585-7632-b697-28e4fd61ef3f","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_08092949d98b672f016ac104ea538c87d28b4ec75dd7eaf8d6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes. I should inspect the CAD geometry directly first. Rendering tests can tell us that removing a part changes pixels, but they do a poor job of explaining whether it is enclosed or visible through an opening.\n\nI’ll check the source solids for openings and enclosed parts, including the head’s movement. Then rendering can serve as a regression check for parts the geometry analysis identifies as safe.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791034602328,"completed_at_ms":1791034605911}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:36:45.914Z","ordinal":17943,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_08092949d98b672f016ac104ea538c87d28b4ec75dd7eaf8d6","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Yes. I should inspect the CAD geometry directly first. Rendering tests can tell us that removing a part changes pixels, but they do a poor job of explaining whether it is enclosed or visible through an opening.\n\nI’ll check the source solids for openings and enclosed parts, including the head’s movement. Then rendering can serve as a regression check for parts the geometry analysis identifies as safe.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a101fa-8585-7632-b697-28e4fd61ef3f","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
