4:     * cite123†trimesh.transformations L135:     * cite124†trimesh.triangles L136:     * cite125†trimesh.typed L137:     * cite126†trimesh.units L138:     * cite127†trimesh.util L139:     * cite128†trimesh.version L140: cite62†Back to top L141: # trimesh.ray.ray_trianglecite129†¶ L142: \nL143: A basic slow implementation of ray- triangle queries.\nL144: \nL145: class trimesh.ray.ray_triangle.RayMeshIntersector(mesh)cite130†¶ L146: \nL147: \nL148: Bases: `object`\nL149: \nL150: An object to query a mesh for ray intersections. Precomputes an r-tree for each triangle on the mesh.\nL151: \nL152: __init__(mesh)cite131†¶ L153: \nL154: \nL155: contains_points(points)cite132†¶ L156: \nL157: \nL158: Check if a mesh contains a list of points, using ray tests.\nL159: \nL160: If the point is on the surface of the mesh the behavior is undefined.\nL161: \nL162: Parameters:\nL163: points ((n, 3) float) – Points in space\nL164: \nL165: Returns:\nL166: \nL167: \nL168: contains – Whether point is inside mesh or not\nL169: \nL170: Return type:\nL171: \nL172: \nL173: (n,) bool\nL174: \nL175: intersects_any(ray_origins, ray_directions, **kwargs)cite133†¶ L176: \nL177: \nL178: Find out if each ray hit any triangle on the mesh.\nL179: \nL180: Parameters:\nL181: \nL182: \nL183:   * ray_origins ((m, 3) float) – Ray origin points\nL184: \nL185:   * ray_directions ((m, 3) float) – Ray direction vectors\nL186: \nL187: Returns:\nL188: \nL189: \nL190: hit – Whether any ray hit any triangle on the mesh\nL191: \nL192: Return type:\nL193: \nL194: \nL195: (m,) bool\nL196: intersects_first(ray_origins, ray_directions, **kwargs)cite134†¶ L197: \nL198: \nL199: Find the index of the first triangle a ray hits.\nL200: \nL201: Parameters:\nL202: \nL203: \nL204:   * ray_origins ((n, 3) float) – Origins of rays\nL205: \nL206:   * ray_directions ((n, 3) float) – Direction (vector) of rays\nL207: \nL208: Returns:\nL209: \nL210: \nL211: triangle_index – Index of triangle ray hit, or -1 if not hit\nL212: \nL213: Return type:\nL214: \nL215: \nL216: (n,) int\nL217: \nL218: intersects_id(ray_origins, ray_directions, return_locations=False, multiple_hits=True, **kwargs)cite135†¶ L219: Find the intersections between the current mesh and an array of rays.\nL220: \nL221: Parameters:\nL222: \nL223: \nL224:   * ray_origins ((m, 3) float) – Ray origin points\nL225: \nL226:   * ray_directions ((m, 3) float) – Ray direction vectors\nL227: \nL228:   * multiple_hits (bool) – Consider multiple hits of each ray or not\nL229: \nL230:   * return_locations (bool) – Return hit locations or not\nL231: \nL232: Returns:\nL233: \nL234: \nL235:   * index_triangle ((h,) int) – Index of triangles hit\nL236: \nL237:   * index_ray ((h,) int) – Index of ray that hit triangle\nL238:   * locations ((h, 3) float) – [optional] Position of intersection in space\nL239: \nL240: intersects_location(ray_origins, ray_directions, **kwargs)cite136†¶ L241: \nL242: \nL243: Return unique cartesian locations where rays hit the mesh. If you are counting the number of hits a ray had, this method should be used as if only the triangle index is used on- edge hits will be counted twice.\nL244: \nL245: Parameters:\nL246: \nL247: \nL248:   * ray_origins ((m, 3) float) – Ray origin points\nL249: \nL250:   * ray_directions ((m, 3) float) – Ray direction vectors\nL251: \nL252: Returns:\nL253:   * locations ((n) sequence of (m,3) float) – Intersection points\nL254: \nL255:   * index_ray ((n,) int) – Array of ray indexes\nL256: \nL257:   * index_tri ((n,) int) – Array of triangle (face) indexes\nL258: \nL259: trimesh.ray.ray_triangle.ray_bounds(ray_origins, ray_directions, bounds, buffer_dist=1e-05)cite137†¶ L260: \nL261: \nL262: Given a set of rays and a bounding box for the volume of interest where the rays will be passing through, find the bounding boxes of the rays as they pass through the volume.\nL263: \nL264: Parameters:\nL265:   * ray_origins ((m,3) float, ray origin points)\nL266: \nL267:   * ray_directions ((m,3) float, ray direction vectors)\nL268: \nL269:   * bounds ((2,3) bounding box (min, max))\nL270: \nL271:   * buffer_dist (float, distance to pad zero width bounding boxes)\nL272: \nL273: Returns:\nL274: \nL275: \nL276: ray_bounding\nL277: \nL278: Return type:\nL279: \nL280: \nL281:   14. set of AABB of rays passing through volume\nL282: \nL283: trimesh.ray.ray_triangle.ray_triangle_candidates(ray_origins, ray_directions, tree)cite138†¶ L284: \nL285: \nL286: Do broad- phase search for triangles that the rays may intersect.\nL287: Does this by creating a bounding box for the ray as it passes through the volume occupied by the tree\nL288: \nL289: Parameters:\nL290: \nL291: \nL292:   * ray_origins ((m, 3) float) – Ray origin points.\nL293: \nL294:   * ray_directions ((m, 3) float) – Ray direction vectors\nL295: \nL296:   * tree (rtree object) – Ccontains AABB of each triangle\nL297: \nL298: Returns:\nL299: \nL300: \nL301:   * ray_candidates ((n,) int) – Triangle indexes\nL302: \nL303:   * ray_id ((n,) int) – Corresponding ray index for a triangle candidate\nL304: trimesh.ray.ray_triangle.ray_triangle_id(triangles, ray_origins, ray_directions, triangles_normal=None, tree=None, multiple_hits=True)cite139†¶ L305: \nL306: \nL307: Find the intersections between a group of triangles and rays\nL308: \nL309: Parameters:\nL310: \nL311: \nL312:   * triangles ((n, 3, 3) float) – Triangles in space\nL313: \nL314:   * ray_origins ((m, 3) float) – Ray origin points\nL315: \nL316:   * ray_directions ((m, 3) float) – Ray direction vectors\nL317: \nL318:   * triangles_normal ((n, 3) float) – Normal vector of triangles, optional\nL319:   * tree (rtree.Index) – Rtree object holding triangle bounds\nL320: \nL321: Returns:\nL322: \nL323: \nL324:   * index_triangle ((h,) int) – Index of triangles hit\nL325: \nL326:   * index_ray ((h,) int) – Index of ray that hit triangle\nL327: \nL328:   * locations ((h, 3) float) – Position of intersection in space\nL329: \nL330: Copyright © 2022, Michael Dawson-Haggerty\nL331: \nL332: Made with cite140†Sphinx†www.sphinx-doc.org and cite141†@pradyunsg†pradyunsg.me 's cite142†Furo†github.com L333: \nL334: On this page\nL335:   * cite62†trimesh.ray.ray_triangle L336:     * cite130†`RayMeshIntersector` --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntrimesh - trimesh 5.1.1 documentation (https://trimesh.org/trimesh.html)\nciteturn64view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://trimesh.org/trimesh.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 5534\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a101fa-8585-7632-b697-28e4fd61ef3f","create_time":1791034695.34524}}}
