{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:44:21.370Z","ordinal":18078,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","turn_id":"01a101fa-8585-7632-b697-28e4fd61ef3f","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_08092949d98b672f016ac106b1fe2c87d2ae04088f310130c9","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Direct geometry analysis has already found something concrete: **6,114 triangles are exact duplicates**, with identical positions, normals and winding. Those can be investigated separately from whole-part removal.\n\nIt also found a line from beneath the assembly that reaches the left motor before the exterior shell. So the motor is not fully enclosed in the exported CAD. I’ve retrieved the original Rhino model as well to inspect its separate objects and openings more precisely.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791035058045,"completed_at_ms":1791035061370}}
