{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:59:02.805Z","ordinal":18317,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1020f-a794-70c0-97c1-5b3937e7d2bb","author":"/root/cad_enclosure_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/cad_enclosure_audit\nPayload:\n**Proved a useful enclosure candidate: 27,756 runtime triangles lie entirely inside retained opaque `Body` shells.**\n\n| Part | Certified interior triangles |\n|---|---:|\n| Motor_Left | 13,412 |\n| Motor_Right | 12,518 |\n| Servo_Head | 1,614 |\n| 01_body | 212 |\n\nSix complete motor components account for 322 of these triangles. Both motors and `Body` share the root transform, so their containment survives every head pose and rigid robot movement.\n\nThe strengthened certificate uses actual runtime Float32 coordinates converted exactly through integer ratios. It verifies:\n\n- Closed, consistently oriented `Body` shells with Euler characteristic 2.\n- Every shell vertex behind every supporting plane, using exact integer arithmetic.\n- Every candidate triangle vertex strictly inside one shell.\n- **At least 0.01 mm clearance**, using an exact squared-distance predicate.\n- Retained enclosure geometry and source/index-file hashes.\n\nBecause each enclosure is convex, the vertex predicates cover entire triangles, not sampled points or camera directions.\n\n`convex-enclosure-certificate.json` and `convex-enclosure-indices.npz` contain the useful result. NPZ SHA256:\n\n`abff2db78779057ce1b3b709d2f6f8f3731a56532a71a5ba895329a58bff22ea`\n\nThe broader rigid-group search found no additional useful strictly convex enclosure. Battery and several electronics surfaces fail strict convexity; I did not relax that requirement.\n\nThis proves geometric containment, conditional on the retained opaque shells and camera/light origins outside them. Shadow-map precision and final pixel preservation remain runtime validation work. No production assets changed; no analysis process remains running."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791035942.804943}}}
