{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:00:10.903Z","ordinal":18335,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a10210-b197-7763-913b-a61b64229430","author":"/root/astra_ultra_final_judge","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/astra_ultra_final_judge\nPayload:\n**Approved as adequate geometric proof for the isolated runtime candidate.**\n\nThe updated code uses exact Float32 rational coordinates and an unbounded-integer squared-distance predicate that correctly certifies the 0.01 mm margin. I verified the script and NPZ hashes against the certificate, the **27,756-triangle union**, and the **504 retained Body-shell triangles**.\n\nApproval assumes unchanged source geometry, transforms, opaque shells and external camera/light positions. Native rendering comparisons remain necessary; this is neither pixel-equivalence nor performance acceptance. I did not rerun the numerical validator."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791036010.903043}}}
