{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:01:58.519Z","ordinal":18356,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a10212-55f7-7601-a66d-b142ef958338","author":"/root/gpu_shader_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/gpu_shader_review\nPayload:\n**Recommend track batching before roughness packing as the next larger-impact test.** It targets a large, concrete concentration of draw and node overhead while retaining every chamfered shoe and rib.\n\nThe checked native inventory contains 228 boxes with 1,452 triangles and 1,176 vertices each: 224 shoes/ribs plus four hub spokes. Shoes/ribs therefore account for **325,248 triangles and 263,424 vertices**, across 224 geometry nodes. Those counts are inventory, not verified draw submissions. Batching would retain those triangles.\n\nRelevant source:\n\n- [TrackBelt.swift:14](/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator/TrackBelt.swift:14): 56 shoes per belt, original box geometry and alternating rib offsets.\n- [TrackBelt.swift:57](/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator/TrackBelt.swift:57): 112 shoe node transforms updated per frame.\n- [TrackLoop.swift:10](/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/apps/simulator-macos/Sources/SimulationCore/TrackLoop.swift:10): Double-precision modulo, straight runs and semicircles.\n- [DirtCoating.swift:33](/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator/DirtCoating.swift:33): geometry-owned surface shader and per-geometry `dirtToBody`.\n- [DirtCoating.swift:97](/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator/DirtCoating.swift:97): coating coordinate calculation; line 114 uses current world position for dune contact.\n\nConcrete design:\n\n1. **Two material batches per belt:** one shoe mesh and one rib mesh, or one geometry with two elements. Copy the actual generated SCNBox sources and original triangle order/winding; do not recreate boxes with lower chamfer segmentation. Retain the continuous carcass mesh.\n2. Each vertex retains its original shoe/rib local position and carries a shoe index. Rib offsets remain the original alternating ±`width*0.23`, Y=`0.004`.\n3. A geometry modifier applies the selected rigid shoe pose to position, normal and any tangent. SceneKit then handles the ordinary node/world/view transforms.\n4. **Start with a CPU-generated pose palette**, using the existing Double `TrackLoop.sample` and verified original node transforms: only 56 matrices per belt. This avoids running modulo, branching and trigonometry separately for hundreds of thousands of vertices in every shadow/AO/main pass. A later compact phase-only GPU version is a separate optimization, requiring numeric validation.\n5. Bind immutable pose data for each frame, preserving lifetime through all passes. Do not overwrite a shared palette while an earlier frame may still read it.\n\nThe crucial coating invariant is **two distinct coordinate systems**:\n\n```text\ncoating reference = initial dirtToBody × original local vertex\ncurrent world     = current root/belt/shoe/rib transform × original local vertex\n```\n\n`TrackBelt.init` calls `update(travel:0)` before `Robot` installs DirtCoating. Therefore `dirtToBody` records each shoe’s **initial pose**. Substituting the current batch coordinate would make the dirt pattern slide or change. Preserve initial coating coordinates through a dedicated varying or equivalent rest-transform palette, while dune-contact calculations use current positions. Preserve `dirtRolling = 0` for these current unnamed belt parts.\n\nOther required invariants and risks:\n\n- Compose the geometry modifier with the existing surface modifier; `DirtCoating.install` currently **replaces** `shaderModifiers` outright.\n- Retain both original materials, sidedness, depth behavior, category masks and shadow eligibility.\n- Set conservative bounds covering the entire animated belt, including all shoe/rib extents. Shader movement must not escape CPU culling bounds.\n- Confirm animation executes consistently in both sun shadow maps, AO preparation and the visible pass.\n- Separate left/right travel, reverse travel, wraparound, paused/reset states and body tilt must remain correct.\n- GPU Float TrackLoop arithmetic is not bit-equivalent to the current Double calculation. Even the palette version can change rounding or coating interpolation; native comparisons remain mandatory.\n\n**Narrow next test:** freeze matched original and batched poses at straight runs, arc boundaries and negative travel; retain a geometry-copy control. Measure actual draw reduction, CPU encoding and GPU envelopes in ABBA blocks, with exact repeat/restoration checks and inspected close-up color/shadow comparisons. Advance to moving belts only after those pass.\n\nRoughness packing targets one measured ground texture lookup and is simpler. Track batching potentially collapses **224 geometry nodes to four material draws per applicable pass**, addressing the measured Marvin encoding cost as well as repeated pass overhead. Actual savings remain unproven: SceneKit might already combine some draws, coarser culling can submit extra vertices, and added vertex shader work can offset savings. The whole-Marvin ~1.2 ms CPU/~2 ms GPU removal result is an upper ceiling, not a belt estimate."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791036118.519723}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:02:17.322Z","ordinal":18357,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ebf8451b-47d8-4e20-92af-8da49a6bba68","process_id":"71755","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat > /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure/generate-convex-candidates.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib,numpy as np\nbase=Path(__file__).parent;root=Path('/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin');resources=root/'apps/simulator-macos/Resources/Marvin';out=base/'convex-candidates';out.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nsha=lambda b:hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()\ncert=json.loads((base/'convex-enclosure-certificate.json').read_text());raw=(resources/'geometry.bin').read_bytes();manifest=json.loads((resources/'manifest.json').read_text())\nassert sha(raw)==cert['geometrySHA256'];assert sha((resources/'manifest.json').read_bytes())==cert['manifestSHA256']\nassert sha((base/'convex-enclosure-indices.npz').read_bytes())==cert['indicesNPZSHA256']\nfor name,key in [('Robot.swift','robotSourceSHA256'),('DirtCoating.swift','dirtSourceSHA256')]:assert sha((root/'apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator'/name).read_bytes())==cert[key]\nselected=np.load(base/'convex-enclosure-indices.npz');rows=[]\nfor p in manifest['parts']:\n groups=[selected[f'{p[\"name\"]}_insideBody{i}'] for i in range(2) if f'{p[\"name\"]}_insideBody{i}' in selected]\n if not groups:continue\n removed=np.unique(np.concatenate(groups))\n if not len(removed):continue\n assert p['name']!='Body';assert removed.min()>=0 and removed.max()<p['triangleCount']\n declared=next(x for x in cert['parts'] if x['name']==p['name'])\n assert len(removed)==declared['containedTriangles']\n assert set(removed.tolist())==set(i for shell in declared['byShell'] for i in shell['faceIndices'])\n original=raw[p['indexOffset']:p['indexOffset']+p['triangleCount']*12];indices=np.frombuffer(original,dtype='<u4').reshape(-1,3)\n keep=np.ones(len(indices),dtype=bool);keep[removed]=False;candidate=indices[keep].tobytes();assert np.array_equal(np.frombuffer(candidate,dtype='<u4').reshape(-1,3),indices[keep])\n (out/(p['name']+'.bin')).write_bytes(candidate)\n rows.append({'part':p['name'],'sourceIndexSHA256':sha(original),'candidateSHA256':sha(candidate),'originalTriangles':len(indices),'candidateTriangles':int(keep.sum()),'removedOriginalTriangleIDs':removed.tolist(),'dataChecks':'Exact union of certificate triangle IDs removed; all remaining index records and all vertex sources unchanged.'})\nassert sum(x['originalTriangles']-x['candidateTriangles'] for x in rows)==27756\n(out/'verification.json').write_text(json.dumps({'sourceSHA256':sha(raw),'method':'Remove only triangles covered by exact convex enclosure certificate; retain all 504 Body shell triangles.','certificateSHA256':sha((base/'convex-enclosure-certificate.json').read_bytes()),'parts':rows},indent=2)+'\\n')\nprint([(r['part'],r['originalTriangles'],r['candidateTriangles']) for r in rows])\nPY\n/Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-analysis-venv/bin/python /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure/generate-convex-candidates.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator/LoadedGPUProbe.swift';s=open(p).read().replace('(variant==\"cad-index-order\" || variant==\"cad-deduplicate\")','[\"cad-index-order\",\"cad-deduplicate\",\"cad-enclosure\"].contains(variant)');open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\napps/simulator-macos/build-app.sh > /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure-probe-build.log 2>&1"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat > /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure/generate-convex-candidates.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib,numpy as np\nbase=Path(__file__).parent;root=Path('/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin');resources=root/'apps/simulator-macos/Resources/Marvin';out=base/'convex-candidates';out.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nsha=lambda b:hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()\ncert=json.loads((base/'convex-enclosure-certificate.json').read_text());raw=(resources/'geometry.bin').read_bytes();manifest=json.loads((resources/'manifest.json').read_text())\nassert sha(raw)==cert['geometrySHA256'];assert sha((resources/'manifest.json').read_bytes())==cert['manifestSHA256']\nassert sha((base/'convex-enclosure-indices.npz').read_bytes())==cert['indicesNPZSHA256']\nfor name,key in [('Robot.swift','robotSourceSHA256'),('DirtCoating.swift','dirtSourceSHA256')]:assert sha((root/'apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator'/name).read_bytes())==cert[key]\nselected=np.load(base/'convex-enclosure-indices.npz');rows=[]\nfor p in manifest['parts']:\n groups=[selected[f'{p[\"name\"]}_insideBody{i}'] for i in range(2) if f'{p[\"name\"]}_insideBody{i}' in selected]\n if not groups:continue\n removed=np.unique(np.concatenate(groups))\n if not len(removed):continue\n assert p['name']!='Body';assert removed.min()>=0 and removed.max()<p['triangleCount']\n declared=next(x for x in cert['parts'] if x['name']==p['name'])\n assert len(removed)==declared['containedTriangles']\n assert set(removed.tolist())==set(i for shell in declared['byShell'] for i in shell['faceIndices'])\n original=raw[p['indexOffset']:p['indexOffset']+p['triangleCount']*12];indices=np.frombuffer(original,dtype='<u4').reshape(-1,3)\n keep=np.ones(len(indices),dtype=bool);keep[removed]=False;candidate=indices[keep].tobytes();assert np.array_equal(np.frombuffer(candidate,dtype='<u4').reshape(-1,3),indices[keep])\n (out/(p['name']+'.bin')).write_bytes(candidate)\n rows.append({'part':p['name'],'sourceIndexSHA256':sha(original),'candidateSHA256':sha(candidate),'originalTriangles':len(indices),'candidateTriangles':int(keep.sum()),'removedOriginalTriangleIDs':removed.tolist(),'dataChecks':'Exact union of certificate triangle IDs removed; all remaining index records and all vertex sources unchanged.'})\nassert sum(x['originalTriangles']-x['candidateTriangles'] for x in rows)==27756\n(out/'verification.json').write_text(json.dumps({'sourceSHA256':sha(raw),'method':'Remove only triangles covered by exact convex enclosure certificate; retain all 504 Body shell triangles.','certificateSHA256':sha((base/'convex-enclosure-certificate.json').read_bytes()),'parts':rows},indent=2)+'\\n')\nprint([(r['part'],r['originalTriangles'],r['candidateTriangles']) for r in rows])\nPY\n/Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-analysis-venv/bin/python /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure/generate-convex-candidates.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator/LoadedGPUProbe.swift';s=open(p).read().replace('(variant==\"cad-index-order\" || variant==\"cad-deduplicate\")','[\"cad-index-order\",\"cad-deduplicate\",\"cad-enclosure\"].contains(variant)');open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\napps/simulator-macos/build-app.sh > /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure-probe-build.log 2>&1"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":61,"nanos":122797833},"formatted_output":""},"started_at_ms":1791036076198,"completed_at_ms":1791036137322}}
