{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:07:15.246Z","ordinal":18417,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_08092949d98b672f016ac10be92ba887d28ecd35616f67421a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_12EHpumtRN5sLBuYzvOSYQUM","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport json,shutil,hashlib,subprocess\\nbase=Path('/Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix');dest=Path('docs/performance-validation/2026-10-03/cad-geometry');dest.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\\nfor run in ['cad-index-clone-control','cad-duplicate-probe-15','cad-enclosure-probe-15']:\\n for file in ['loaded-gpu-probe.json','image-comparison.json']:\\n  shutil.copy2(base/run/file,dest/(run+'-'+file))\\n# This binary is only assigned to the last run; earlier binaries were replaced.\\nbinary=Path('apps/simulator-macos/.build/Marvin Simulator.app/Contents/MacOS/MarvinSimulator');(dest/'enclosure-run-source.json').write_text(json.dumps({'head':subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],text=True).strip(),'binarySHA256':hashlib.sha256(binary.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'scope':'cad-enclosure-probe-15 only; release build includes uncommitted opt-in diagnostic code and preexisting prototypes. Frozen GPU command-buffer envelope, not sustained/display timing.'},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\np=Path('docs/renderer-study.md')\\nwith p.open('a') as f:f.write('''\\n\\n### October 3: direct CAD enclosure and controlled index experiments\\n\\nFollowing the user's correction, geometry is analyzed before using full-scene\\nrendering as regression evidence. Native Rhino and tessellated STEP audits found\\nopen/nonmanifold exterior meshes, so global point-in-solid classification is not\\nvalid without additional proof. Bounding boxes and sampled rays are insufficient.\\nOne direct neutral-CAD ray reaches Motor_Left from below; this disproves complete\\nenclosure of that whole part in the exported CAD (procedural runtime belts are\\nnot part of this ray test).\\n\\nExact Float32 position+normal comparison found 6,114 same-winding duplicate\\ntriangles. A stronger enclosure certificate identifies 27,756 triangles wholly\\ninside two retained convex `Body` components: Motor_Left 13,412; Motor_Right\\n12,518; Servo_Head 1,614; 01_body 212. All 504 enclosing Body triangles remain.\\nThe exact rational/integer proof checks closed topology, convex halfspaces and\\nat least 0.01 mm clearance. These parts share the same rigid parent and opaque\\nmaterials. Astra Ultra reviewed the corrected exact-representability and margin\\npredicates. This is geometric containment, not pixel or performance acceptance.\\n\\nNative diagnostic comparisons use clear midday town, M2, 1920×1080, 2× MSAA,\\nproduction shadow batching, 15 seconds of driving followed by frozen ABBA blocks.\\nEach block retains 60 GPU/encoding samples after 30 warmup frames. Runtime source\\ngeometry and original/candidate index hashes bind every loaded candidate to its\\noffline verification manifest. An original-index geometry reconstruction control\\nseparates reconstruction effects from changed index content.\\n\\n- Original-index reconstruction: exact images in all three experiments.\\n- Vertex-cache index reorder: 11.142/11.162 ms versus bracketing original\\n  11.324/11.333 ms GPU medians. 780 pixels changed, maximum channel delta 10/255;\\n  unchanged triangle tuples/winding do not imply identical depth-tie pixels.\\n- Exact duplicate removal: no consistent GPU benefit (11.600/11.514 versus\\n  11.497/11.517 ms); 16 pixels changed by at most 1/255. Not promoted.\\n- Certified enclosed triangles: 11.368/11.364 versus 11.416/11.436 ms;\\n  about 0.06 ms difference is too small to establish sustained benefit.\\n  74 pixels changed by at most 4/255. Not promoted.\\n\\nThe candidate images were inspected. All restored production images match their\\ninitial references exactly in these three tests. Raw timing samples and pixel\\ncounts are in [CAD geometry evidence](performance-validation/2026-10-03/cad-geometry/).\\nNo production geometry changed, no ten-minute acceptance result is claimed, and\\nall earlier full-quality sustained/headroom requirements remain open.\\n\\nNext larger attribution target: Marvin's 224 separate shoe/rib geometry nodes.\\nThey contain 325,248 triangles; an exact-pose batching experiment must preserve\\nthose triangles and the coating's original rest coordinates, then measure actual\\ndraw, encoding and GPU changes before attempting animated batching.\\n''')\\nPY\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin\",\"max_output_tokens\":700}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791036368.59768}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:07:15.305Z","ordinal":18418,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","session_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","root_turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","response_id":"resp_08092949d98b672f016ac10bcf538c87d2a4098ae2043df0e9","usage":{"input_tokens":192477,"cached_input_tokens":191488,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1552,"reasoning_output_tokens":516,"total_tokens":194029},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6335075,"cached_input_tokens":6308224,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15760,"reasoning_output_tokens":7030,"total_tokens":6350835},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":313896490,"cached_input_tokens":309528192,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":920919,"reasoning_output_tokens":319731,"total_tokens":314817409}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:07:15.380Z","ordinal":18419,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f0281134-8637-44c9-940b-0a1a84ad03a4","process_id":"39372","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,shutil,hashlib,subprocess\nbase=Path('/Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix');dest=Path('docs/performance-validation/2026-10-03/cad-geometry');dest.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nfor run in ['cad-index-clone-control','cad-duplicate-probe-15','cad-enclosure-probe-15']:\n for file in ['loaded-gpu-probe.json','image-comparison.json']:\n  shutil.copy2(base/run/file,dest/(run+'-'+file))\n# This binary is only assigned to the last run; earlier binaries were replaced.\nbinary=Path('apps/simulator-macos/.build/Marvin Simulator.app/Contents/MacOS/MarvinSimulator');(dest/'enclosure-run-source.json').write_text(json.dumps({'head':subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],text=True).strip(),'binarySHA256':hashlib.sha256(binary.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'scope':'cad-enclosure-probe-15 only; release build includes uncommitted opt-in diagnostic code and preexisting prototypes. Frozen GPU command-buffer envelope, not sustained/display timing.'},indent=2)+'\\n')\np=Path('docs/renderer-study.md')\nwith p.open('a') as f:f.write('''\n\n### October 3: direct CAD enclosure and controlled index experiments\n\nFollowing the user's correction, geometry is analyzed before using full-scene\nrendering as regression evidence. Native Rhino and tessellated STEP audits found\nopen/nonmanifold exterior meshes, so global point-in-solid classification is not\nvalid without additional proof. Bounding boxes and sampled rays are insufficient.\nOne direct neutral-CAD ray reaches Motor_Left from below; this disproves complete\nenclosure of that whole part in the exported CAD (procedural runtime belts are\nnot part of this ray test).\n\nExact Float32 position+normal comparison found 6,114 same-winding duplicate\ntriangles. A stronger enclosure certificate identifies 27,756 triangles wholly\ninside two retained convex `Body` components: Motor_Left 13,412; Motor_Right\n12,518; Servo_Head 1,614; 01_body 212. All 504 enclosing Body triangles remain.\nThe exact rational/integer proof checks closed topology, convex halfspaces and\nat least 0.01 mm clearance. These parts share the same rigid parent and opaque\nmaterials. Astra Ultra reviewed the corrected exact-representability and margin\npredicates. This is geometric containment, not pixel or performance acceptance.\n\nNative diagnostic comparisons use clear midday town, M2, 1920×1080, 2× MSAA,\nproduction shadow batching, 15 seconds of driving followed by frozen ABBA blocks.\nEach block retains 60 GPU/encoding samples after 30 warmup frames. Runtime source\ngeometry and original/candidate index hashes bind every loaded candidate to its\noffline verification manifest. An original-index geometry reconstruction control\nseparates reconstruction effects from changed index content.\n\n- Original-index reconstruction: exact images in all three experiments.\n- Vertex-cache index reorder: 11.142/11.162 ms versus bracketing original\n  11.324/11.333 ms GPU medians. 780 pixels changed, maximum channel delta 10/255;\n  unchanged triangle tuples/winding do not imply identical depth-tie pixels.\n- Exact duplicate removal: no consistent GPU benefit (11.600/11.514 versus\n  11.497/11.517 ms); 16 pixels changed by at most 1/255. Not promoted.\n- Certified enclosed triangles: 11.368/11.364 versus 11.416/11.436 ms;\n  about 0.06 ms difference is too small to establish sustained benefit.\n  74 pixels changed by at most 4/255. Not promoted.\n\nThe candidate images were inspected. All restored production images match their\ninitial references exactly in these three tests. Raw timing samples and pixel\ncounts are in [CAD geometry evidence](performance-validation/2026-10-03/cad-geometry/).\nNo production geometry changed, no ten-minute acceptance result is claimed, and\nall earlier full-quality sustained/headroom requirements remain open.\n\nNext larger attribution target: Marvin's 224 separate shoe/rib geometry nodes.\nThey contain 325,248 triangles; an exact-pose batching experiment must preserve\nthose triangles and the coating's original rest coordinates, then measure actual\ndraw, encoding and GPU changes before attempting animated batching.\n''')\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,shutil,hashlib,subprocess\nbase=Path('/Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix');dest=Path('docs/performance-validation/2026-10-03/cad-geometry');dest.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nfor run in ['cad-index-clone-control','cad-duplicate-probe-15','cad-enclosure-probe-15']:\n for file in ['loaded-gpu-probe.json','image-comparison.json']:\n  shutil.copy2(base/run/file,dest/(run+'-'+file))\n# This binary is only assigned to the last run; earlier binaries were replaced.\nbinary=Path('apps/simulator-macos/.build/Marvin Simulator.app/Contents/MacOS/MarvinSimulator');(dest/'enclosure-run-source.json').write_text(json.dumps({'head':subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],text=True).strip(),'binarySHA256':hashlib.sha256(binary.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'scope':'cad-enclosure-probe-15 only; release build includes uncommitted opt-in diagnostic code and preexisting prototypes. Frozen GPU command-buffer envelope, not sustained/display timing.'},indent=2)+'\\n')\np=Path('docs/renderer-study.md')\nwith p.open('a') as f:f.write('''\n\n### October 3: direct CAD enclosure and controlled index experiments\n\nFollowing the user's correction, geometry is analyzed before using full-scene\nrendering as regression evidence. Native Rhino and tessellated STEP audits found\nopen/nonmanifold exterior meshes, so global point-in-solid classification is not\nvalid without additional proof. Bounding boxes and sampled rays are insufficient.\nOne direct neutral-CAD ray reaches Motor_Left from below; this disproves complete\nenclosure of that whole part in the exported CAD (procedural runtime belts are\nnot part of this ray test).\n\nExact Float32 position+normal comparison found 6,114 same-winding duplicate\ntriangles. A stronger enclosure certificate identifies 27,756 triangles wholly\ninside two retained convex `Body` components: Motor_Left 13,412; Motor_Right\n12,518; Servo_Head 1,614; 01_body 212. All 504 enclosing Body triangles remain.\nThe exact rational/integer proof checks closed topology, convex halfspaces and\nat least 0.01 mm clearance. These parts share the same rigid parent and opaque\nmaterials. Astra Ultra reviewed the corrected exact-representability and margin\npredicates. This is geometric containment, not pixel or performance acceptance.\n\nNative diagnostic comparisons use clear midday town, M2, 1920×1080, 2× MSAA,\nproduction shadow batching, 15 seconds of driving followed by frozen ABBA blocks.\nEach block retains 60 GPU/encoding samples after 30 warmup frames. Runtime source\ngeometry and original/candidate index hashes bind every loaded candidate to its\noffline verification manifest. An original-index geometry reconstruction control\nseparates reconstruction effects from changed index content.\n\n- Original-index reconstruction: exact images in all three experiments.\n- Vertex-cache index reorder: 11.142/11.162 ms versus bracketing original\n  11.324/11.333 ms GPU medians. 780 pixels changed, maximum channel delta 10/255;\n  unchanged triangle tuples/winding do not imply identical depth-tie pixels.\n- Exact duplicate removal: no consistent GPU benefit (11.600/11.514 versus\n  11.497/11.517 ms); 16 pixels changed by at most 1/255. Not promoted.\n- Certified enclosed triangles: 11.368/11.364 versus 11.416/11.436 ms;\n  about 0.06 ms difference is too small to establish sustained benefit.\n  74 pixels changed by at most 4/255. Not promoted.\n\nThe candidate images were inspected. All restored production images match their\ninitial references exactly in these three tests. Raw timing samples and pixel\ncounts are in [CAD geometry evidence](performance-validation/2026-10-03/cad-geometry/).\nNo production geometry changed, no ten-minute acceptance result is claimed, and\nall earlier full-quality sustained/headroom requirements remain open.\n\nNext larger attribution target: Marvin's 224 separate shoe/rib geometry nodes.\nThey contain 325,248 triangles; an exact-pose batching experiment must preserve\nthose triangles and the coating's original rest coordinates, then measure actual\ndraw, encoding and GPU changes before attempting animated batching.\n''')\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2833},"formatted_output":""},"started_at_ms":1791036435380,"completed_at_ms":1791036435380}}
