{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:07:53.082Z","ordinal":18433,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","session_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","root_turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","response_id":"resp_08092949d98b672f016ac10c2ed8e887d2b86a8f3c4a932149","usage":{"input_tokens":199210,"cached_input_tokens":194048,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":117,"reasoning_output_tokens":100,"total_tokens":199327},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6728379,"cached_input_tokens":6694656,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16072,"reasoning_output_tokens":7247,"total_tokens":6744451},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":314289794,"cached_input_tokens":309914624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":921231,"reasoning_output_tokens":319948,"total_tokens":315211025}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:07:53.084Z","ordinal":18434,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a10217-befc-7253-93af-ffe8a4a3e83e","call_id":"call_1bktAMfFFNf1C4jgDgOgJ8id","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/astra_ultra_final_judge\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**Approved as adequate geometric proof for the isolated runtime candidate.**\\n\\nThe updated code uses exact Float32 rational coordinates and an unbounded-integer squared-distance predicate that correctly certifies the 0.01 mm margin. I verified the script and NPZ hashes against the certificate, the **27,756-triangle union**, and the **504 retained Body-shell triangles**.\\n\\nApproval assumes unchanged source geometry, transforms, opaque shells and external camera/light positions. Native rendering comparisons remain necessary; this is neither pixel-equivalence nor performance acceptance. I did not rerun the numerical validator.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/astra_ultra_final_judge/render_hotpaths\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**I found no counterexample to the proposed cone bound for the guarded path.** The earlier projection-amplification example is now excluded.\\n\\nFor identical stored normals, projection is fixed and linear. Matching quantized unit directions differ by at most approximately **√3/65536 = 2.643×10⁻⁵ radians, or 0.00152°**, plus floating-point error. Positive-weight accumulation cannot move the resulting direction outside that cone. Keying both directions and requiring orientation magnitude above 0.25 also prevents a handedness reversal.\\n\\nTwo qualifications remain:\\n\\n- **SceneKit assumption:** this bounds the gradients calculated here and their positive-weight accumulation. The repository’s exporter uses that construction; SceneKit’s internal tangent generator still needs native image verification.\\n- **Fallback namespace:** exact fallback vectors and quantized directions share the same key representation. A theoretical boundary case can collide when rounding moves an orientation just above 0.25 to just below it. That violates the comment’s strict “retain the exact key” separation, but the colliding directions remain close; it does **not** defeat the cone bound. A mode bit would make the separation explicit. I have not established such a collision in current town geometry.\\n\\nKeep the earlier degenerate/projection fixtures as exclusion tests, then compare original triangle-soup rendering against this candidate on close-up normal-mapped surfaces. There is no source-backed reason here to reject the guarded prototype.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/audio_judge\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Interim verdict: substantial improvement, but fix these before acceptance:\\n\\n1. **Assisted braking incorrectly retains boost audio.** The audio reads only manual `brake`; corner assistance applies `assistedBrakePressure` while leaving boost/throttle set.\\n2. **Quick boost taps lose release cues.** The 180 ms cooldown suppresses edges but still updates `previousBoost`, permanently discarding the event.\\n3. **Boost tests can falsely pass.** Counters persist across resets, include player events, and increment when no one-shot slot is available. Current `aiBoostAudible` does not establish audible AI boosting.\\n4. **Postrace storm perspective is inconsistent.** Listener moves to the fixed track center, but wind/shelter still follows the departing player.\\n5. **`ambience:false` leaves town ambience enabled.**\\n6. **Documentation still describes the superseded implementation.**\\n\\nRemaining review should inspect native renders and lifecycle/performance evidence. I have not heard the audio and cannot certify perceived AAA quality.\\n\\nThe agent inventory exposes names/status only; it does not independently expose model or effort settings.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/cad_enclosure_audit\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/gpu_shader_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791036473.084824}}}
