{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:16:33.404Z","ordinal":18501,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1021f-af7c-7480-860f-f5965e9cf2b7","author":"/root/gpu_shader_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/gpu_shader_review\nPayload:\nImplemented the frozen prototype at [TrackBatchProbe.swift](/Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/TrackBatchProbe.swift). No repository files changed; no build or native run performed.\n\nIntegration:\n\n```swift\nlet trackProbe = try TrackBatchProbe(root: robot.root, tracks: robot.tracks)\ntry trackProbe.setMode(.original)     // unchanged native geometry\ntry trackProbe.setMode(.copyControl)  // new wrappers, unchanged sources/elements\ntry trackProbe.setMode(.batch)        // four frozen batches\n// or: try trackProbe.setEnabled(true)\nlet report = trackProbe.statistics\n```\n\nConstruct after DirtCoating installation with simulation stopped and the pose settled. Retain the object through comparison; deinitialization restores geometry/visibility and removes proxies.\n\nThe prototype:\n\n- Selects exactly 56 shoes and 56 child ribs per belt through `robot.tracks`; excludes carcasses and hubs.\n- Preserves all vertices, triangles, winding and UV bytes.\n- Bakes current positions, inverse-transpose normals and transformed tangents into belt-local geometry.\n- Preserves each original cached `dirtToBody` coordinate through a float varying. The current-world dune-contact expression remains unchanged.\n- Produces separate shoe/rib batches per belt with original materials.\n- Rejects unsupported geometry/layout, mismatched materials/uniforms, animation, pivots and changed frozen transforms.\n- Reports counts, all source transforms, and position/normal/tangent/rest-coordinate component errors against Double evaluation of captured Float matrices.\n\nNative validation still needs to establish shader compilation, copy-control equivalence, reference/restoration equivalence and actual timing. Particular risks are Float baking versus SceneKit transform rounding, rest-coordinate interpolation, the added color stream used for that varying, and changed draw/culling order. The modifier resets geometry color to white after reading the varying, but that behavior still needs native verification.\n\nThis deliberately supplies **no dynamic pose update**. Any shoe movement requires constructing a new frozen probe."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791036993.404409}}}
