{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:19:59.967Z","ordinal":18602,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a10222-d65f-73f2-a34f-0ab36fef5c89","author":"/root/astra_ultra_final_judge","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/astra_ultra_final_judge\nPayload:\n**Adequate repeatable geometric proof for the isolated candidate.** No blocking defect found.\n\n- Exact integer arithmetic validates every selected vertex’s containment and clearance; the floating-point prefilter cannot create false acceptances.\n- Shell checks cover closure, winding, connectivity, vertex links and convexity. All 504 Body triangles are explicitly retained.\n- Saved hashes match the verifier, index archive, manifest and inspected runtime sources. Selection remains **27,756 triangles**.\n- Negative fixtures meaningfully test open, nonconvex, reversed, duplicate and inconsistently wound shells, plus boundary/clearance failures.\n\nOne useful regression addition: an oblique shell with different non-unit coordinate scales would exercise the full distance predicate beyond axis-aligned cubes.\n\nRuntime opacity and relative transforms remain manually reviewed conditions; hashes do not enforce them. This approves geometric candidate selection—not raster equivalence or sustained performance. I did not execute the verifier or self-tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791037199.967598}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:20:27.363Z","ordinal":18603,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_08092949d98b672f016ac10f1416f487d2bd314157f055f394","status":"completed","call_id":"call_xudf6k00eGeAbzhCbxmOcsNi","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/scripts/rendering/check-cad-enclosure.py\\n@@\\n     assert exact_inside(mixed.mean(axis=0)[None], shell, Fraction(1,4)).all()\\n+    # Exact 3-4-5 rotation plus scale: the oblique plane normal has length 5,\\n+    # rather than 1. Shell integers use scale 8; these point integers use 32.\\n+    # The near face is 5/8 from the centre, so t=1/2 leaves 5/16 clearance\\n+    # (passes 1/4), t=3/4 leaves 5/32 (fails), and t>=1 is not strictly inside.\\n+    oblique_transform = np.asarray([[3,-4,0], [4,3,0], [0,0,5]]) / 8\\n+    oblique = certify_shell(vertices @ oblique_transform.T, faces)\\n+    oblique_points = np.asarray([[t,0,0] for t in [0, .5, .75, 1, 1.25]]) @ oblique_transform.T\\n+    _, oblique_point_scale = exact_coordinates(oblique_points)\\n+    assert oblique[\\\"integerScale\\\"] == 8 and oblique_point_scale == 32\\n+    assert exact_inside(oblique_points, oblique, Fraction(1,4)).tolist() == [True, True, False, False, False]\\n@@\\n-                      \\\"otherFixtures\\\": [\\\"mixed coordinate scales\\\", \\\"outside triangle vertex\\\", \\\"two components\\\"]}))\\n+                      \\\"otherFixtures\\\": [\\\"mixed coordinate scales\\\", \\\"oblique shell and unequal non-unit scales\\\", \\\"outside triangle vertex\\\", \\\"two components\\\"]}))\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"/Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-analysis-venv/bin/python scripts/rendering/check-cad-enclosure.py --self-test --output /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure/reusable-verifier > /Users/thomi/Projects/marvin-town-planning/sustained-fix/cad-enclosure/reusable-verifier.log 2>&1\",workdir:\"/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:2500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791037202.339778}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:20:27.381Z","ordinal":18604,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0fd98-2f5c-78c3-9769-86fbf8a6fc22","turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-e054b153-ed4d-45c2-b408-a5e76cb56999","changes":{"/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/scripts/rendering/check-cad-enclosure.py":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -310,2 +310,12 @@\n     assert exact_inside(mixed.mean(axis=0)[None], shell, Fraction(1,4)).all()\n+    # Exact 3-4-5 rotation plus scale: the oblique plane normal has length 5,\n+    # rather than 1. Shell integers use scale 8; these point integers use 32.\n+    # The near face is 5/8 from the centre, so t=1/2 leaves 5/16 clearance\n+    # (passes 1/4), t=3/4 leaves 5/32 (fails), and t>=1 is not strictly inside.\n+    oblique_transform = np.asarray([[3,-4,0], [4,3,0], [0,0,5]]) / 8\n+    oblique = certify_shell(vertices @ oblique_transform.T, faces)\n+    oblique_points = np.asarray([[t,0,0] for t in [0, .5, .75, 1, 1.25]]) @ oblique_transform.T\n+    _, oblique_point_scale = exact_coordinates(oblique_points)\n+    assert oblique[\"integerScale\"] == 8 and oblique_point_scale == 32\n+    assert exact_inside(oblique_points, oblique, Fraction(1,4)).tolist() == [True, True, False, False, False]\n     failures = []\n@@ -327,3 +337,3 @@\n                       \"pointFixtures\": [\"inside\", \"exact margin\", \"insufficient margin\", \"boundary\", \"outside\"],\n-                      \"otherFixtures\": [\"mixed coordinate scales\", \"outside triangle vertex\", \"two components\"]}))\n+                      \"otherFixtures\": [\"mixed coordinate scales\", \"oblique shell and unequal non-unit scales\", \"outside triangle vertex\", \"two components\"]}))\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/scripts/rendering/check-cad-enclosure.py\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791037227380,"completed_at_ms":1791037227381}}
