{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:22:54.247Z","ordinal":18661,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a10225-7f27-71a0-89e7-6fcb4240ac55","author":"/root/gpu_shader_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/gpu_shader_review\nPayload:\n**Use local transforms directly, then retain batching as an opt-in CPU optimization experiment. GPU benefit remains unproven.**\n\nAt [TrackBatchProbe.swift:162](/Users/thomi/Projects/entireio-marvin/apps/simulator-macos/Sources/MarvinSimulator/TrackBatchProbe.swift:162), replace the world-mediated conversion with the already verified hierarchy:\n\n```swift\nlet current: simd_float4x4\nif node.parent === parent {\n    current = node.simdTransform             // shoe → belt\n} else if let shoe = node.parent, shoe.parent === parent {\n    current = shoe.simdTransform * node.simdTransform // rib → shoe → belt\n} else {\n    throw Failure(\"Unexpected frozen belt hierarchy\")\n}\n```\n\nKeep the identity-pivot guards. Do not include the belt’s own transform: the batch is already its child. **Keep `cachedRest.scnMatrix4Value` unchanged**; recomputing the coating reference would change the baseline semantics.\n\nThe saved report shows shoe X translations reaching **+7.6293945×10⁻⁶**, although their direct local X is zero. It also introduces tiny off-axis rotation terms. The present ~1.5×10⁻⁸ “position error” measures arithmetic using this already perturbed matrix, so it misses the conversion error. Add a separate comparison against the direct local chain.\n\nThe 2,365 changed pixels do not identify one cause:\n\n- 1,532 occur in rows 726–759, around Marvin’s tracks.\n- 2,051 differ by only 1/255; maximum 6/255 occurs at `(1029,753)`.\n- The batch repeats match one another, while restoration changes 30 pixels elsewhere.\n- I viewed the full native reference/candidate pair; no obvious missing track detail is visible at this scale.\n\nThe rest-coordinate varying is mathematically equivalent to the original affine reconstruction, but changes interpolation, rounding and operation order. The extra color stream could also change shader specialization. Neither is isolated by the existing copy control.\n\nTwo narrow controls would distinguish these:\n\n1. **Color-carrier control:** original 224 nodes/positions/materials; add the color stream and geometry modifier, but retain the original surface coordinate expression.\n2. **Rest-varying control:** same unchanged nodes/positions, then switch only the surface reference to the new varying.\n\nRun these after fixing the local-chain conversion. This separates shader/coordinate effects from baking and merging. Retain exact repeat/restoration checks; do not attribute their residuals to a specific cause without evidence.\n\nThe encoding reduction is substantial: approximately **2.73 → 1.71 ms**, around **38%**, measured as elapsed encoding time—not exclusive CPU execution or energy. GPU medians are bracket-dependent and show no reliable gain. A dynamic palette version is worth a bounded trial, provided it:\n\n- Keeps cached rest coordinates and all geometry.\n- Uses existing Double TrackLoop calculations for the initial pose palette.\n- Avoids per-vertex trigonometry.\n- Measures the added palette/vertex work and rejects a meaningful GPU regression.\n\nThis may relieve CPU scheduling or thermal load, but the current frozen result does **not** establish either effect or move the GPU headroom target by itself. No files changed or workloads started."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10203-cbf2-7142-9114-67ec5e108a8c","create_time":1791037374.24757}}}
